 "text": "Hello there! How's your day? Keep a lookout on both sides and always stop if someone is arriving. Pick a path that gives you enough warning and that you can always see you. Tell them to slow down and wave them through. Most people appreciate a clear path. stops and waits for traffic to stop completely before going. It only takes few seconds and makes the quiet sign much less useful. It is at first, but it' worth doing. Lots of accidents at junctions happen because people push forward to see traffic while the car in front is still moving.",
